---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Thomas Miller"
  description="Background, philosophy, and the tools behind this quiet corner of the web."
  currentPath="/about"
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="section-label">BACKGROUND & PHILOSOPHY</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">
        I am an essayist, interface designer, and researcher exploring the intersection of digital minimalism, calm software, and analog thinking tools.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div class="prose content-section">
      <p>
        For over a decade, I worked in commercial software product design. During that period, I observed an industry increasingly captivated by extractive metrics: monthly active users, notification velocity, and time-in-app.
      </p>

      <p>
        <em>Many things one mind</em> is an inquiry into alternatives. What would computing feel like if tools were designed to be closed rather than perpetually scrolled? What if digital surfaces honored the tactile, quiet permanence of paper?
      </p>

      <h2>Core Design Convictions</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Quietness as a First Principle</strong>: Software should never speak unless spoken to. Ambient silence is the prerequisite for rigorous contemplation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Tactile Restraint</strong>: Warm tones, visible negative space, and disciplined typography reduce optical strain and aesthetic anxiety.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analog Complements</strong>: Digital tools excel at search, transmission, and indexing; physical tools excel at synthesis, memory retention, and deliberate composition. The healthy life balances both.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <blockquote>
        "The highest virtue of a tool is not its novelty, but how gracefully it steps out of the way when the human begins to think."
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Colophon</h2>

      <p>
        This site is published statically using <strong>Astro</strong>. The typographic hierarchy pairs <strong>Aleo</strong> for literary titles and body text with <strong>JetBrains Mono</strong> for dates, metadata, and code structures.
      </p>

      <p>
        Color palettes are inspired by unbleached cotton rag paper, burnt sienna pigments, and iron gall ink. No trackers, telemetry scripts, or cookies are loaded on this domain.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .page-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .divider {
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--border-muted);
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  .content-section {
    width: 100%;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-title {
      font-size: 2.2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
